  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CREATION OF THE COMMUNITY RESERVE OF CHINATU, CHIHUAHUA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners will implement the following large-scale protection mechanisms: 1) Implementation of a mix of legal instruments to protect critical habitats for migratory birds, such as developing the Ejido Chinatu Forestry Management Plan (145,000 ha), zoning and segregation of forestry use in at least 30,000 hectares of forests with High Values for Conservation and strengthening the protection of segregated forests by negotiating an Ejido Reserve with ejido authorities. Partners will present a proposal before CONANP for this Ejido Reserve to be designated as a Voluntary Conservation Area, which can facilitate financing of conservation activities. 2) Restoration of 800 hectares through direct reforestation and soils conservation complementary works to recuperate the forest. 3) Building local capacities through training, environmental education, and increase awareness in key audiences for the conservation of forests.</narrative>
  </description>
